{
  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only single-profile with scvi_n200 achieves 0.520 accuracy (vs 0.485 for PCA-2000), confirming RNA as the dominant modality and scvi_n200 as the current best encoder. Image-only is weak (0.208). The multiprofile axis is completely unexplored—zero experiments have tested whether aggregating multiple profiles per cell adds signal. Question: config_005 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) isolates the effect of the multiprofile+aggregation design decision while holding the encoder at the currently best performer (scvi_n200). avgpool is the simplest aggregation, making this a clean first test of whether multiprofile helps at all. Why this is the best next experiment: (1) it opens a completely new axis with no prior information, which is more informative than a third encoder comparison (scgpt) where the PCA→scvi gain was already modest (~3.5 pts), suggesting we may be near the single-profile RNA ceiling; (2) if multiprofile+avgpool yields a meaningful gain, it justifies testing transformer aggregation (config_006) and multiprofile variants of other encoders; if it does not help, we can deprioritize the entire multiprofile branch and save budget; (3) it uses the best-known encoder, so any gain or loss is attributable to the profile/aggregation decision rather than confounded by a weaker representation."
}

